== Reinforcement Learning Task Formulation <sec:rl_tasks>

Two progressive #ac("RL") tasks are defined on the validated robot model. The _reach_ task tests fundamental motion control across actuation modes. The _cube place_ task extends reach to a full manipulation sequence including grasping, transport, and release. Both tasks share a common simulation environment and use the manager-based #ac("MDP") workflow provided by IsaacLab~@isaaclab_task_design_workflows.

Both tasks are formulated against the tendon-driven arm as their fixed reference, in line with the role of the arm as the only physical subsystem of the manipulator (see @sec:physical_robot). The base and the gripper enter the task definitions only through the modular robot configuration: observations, actions, and rewards are written so that the prismatic base or the parallel-jaw gripper can be replaced by an alternative subsystem without rewriting the task itself, which is important for re-using these tasks on future iterations of the platform.

=== Simulation Environment <subsec:sim_env>

All tasks share a common base scene configuration (`ProjBaseSceneCfg`) that provides the physical environment for conveyor-based manipulation. @tab:scene_elements summarizes the scene elements.

